      "writtenOn": "2026-08-20T18:02:30Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "**Architecture \u0026 Main Thread Overhead**:\n`onJankData()` runs on SurfaceFlinger\u0027s main compositor thread upon frame completion. Offloading all processing to `BackgroundExecutor::getLowPriorityInstance()` is an intentional design choice:\n- Jank reporting is asynchronous and telemetry-focused; it is not on the latency-critical display path.\n- Performing hash lookups (`mJankListeners.count(layerId)`), map allocations (`mJankData.emplace()`), and cache bouncing on `mLock` / `mJankDataLock` on the main thread adds latency and jitter to the compositor.\n- The `sListenerCount \u003d\u003d 0` atomic fast-path already provides near-zero overhead when no listeners are active.\n\n*(Generated by Jetski)*",
      "revId": "5a4a98160f208460031299168db6e4e2e338e1f0",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
