      "writtenOn": "2026-08-20T18:02:30Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "**Thread Safety \u0026 RAII Guidelines**:\nUsing manual `.lock()` and `.unlock()` instead of RAII guards (such as `std::unique_lock\u003cstd::mutex\u003e lk(tracker.mLock, std::try_to_lock)`) violates Android C++ coding standards and bypasses Clang thread-safety annotations (`GUARDED_BY(mLock)`).\n\nAdditionally, if `mLock.try_lock()` succeeds but `mJankDataLock.try_lock()` fails on line 79, the lock state becomes asymmetrical.\n\n*(Generated by Jetski)*",
      "revId": "5a4a98160f208460031299168db6e4e2e338e1f0",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
