      "writtenOn": "2026-08-20T18:02:30Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "`const gui::JankData\u0026\u0026` is a const rvalue reference:\n1. Because it is `const`, passing `jankData` to `mJankData.emplace(layerId, jankData)` will NOT move from it; it will copy-construct instead.\n2. In `onJankData()`, if `processJankData(..., true)` returns `false`, `data` is subsequently captured into the background lambda via `data \u003d std::move(data)`. If `processJankData` had actually moved from the argument, this would lead to a use-after-move bug.\n\nIf this helper is kept, consider passing `gui::JankData` by value or `const gui::JankData\u0026`.\n\n*(Generated by Jetski)*",
